direction: down

title: |md
  ## NAPI: cooperative polled RX
| {near: top-center; shape: text}

before: "Pure-IRQ era (pre-NAPI)" {
  style.fill: "#fee2e2"
  b_body: |md
    Every packet → one IRQ → driver runs RX in IRQ context.

    **Problem at high rates:**
    - 1 Mpps = 1M IRQs/s
    - Receive livelock — CPU spends all time in IRQ
    - Other work starves
  |
}

napi: "NAPI hybrid (modern)" {
  style.fill: "#dcfce7"
  n_body: |md
    First packet → IRQ → napi_schedule() raises softirq.
    Driver disables further IRQs. Polls until budget exhausted.

    **Wins:**
    - One IRQ per burst, not per packet
    - Bounded work (`napi->poll(napi, budget)`)
    - Caller (softirq) yields when budget hit
    - Re-enables IRQs only when no more work
  |
}

budget: |md
  **Budget mechanism:**
  - Default: `net.core.netdev_budget = 300` (packets per softirq run)
  - `netdev_budget_usecs = 2000` (max 2ms per softirq run)
  - Hit either limit → return early, reschedule
  - Polling continues on next softirq tick
| {shape: callout; style.fill: "#fef3c7"}

before -> napi: "evolved" {style.stroke-dash: 4}
napi -> budget
